# Architecture Docs Maintenance (Workspace)

## Directory Layout

| Directory | Contents | Write authority |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/architecture/*.md` | Subsystem docs (one per overhaul target) | `/overhaul` only — ¬direct edits |
| `docs/architecture/appendices/` | Cross-cutting reference (config, tools, libs, events) | `/doc-check` factual corrections via `StrReplace` |
| `docs/architecture/design/` | Historical design docs and proposals | User-directed only |

## Subsystem Docs — Write Authority (CRITICAL)

**Invariant**: ∀ files in `docs/architecture/*.md`: written ONLY via `/overhaul {service_dir}`

The `/overhaul` command runs `doc-generate` (extract docstrings → draft → review → merge).
Direct writes by the agent — even accurate ones — bypass this pipeline and create:
- Docs not grounded in source docstrings (will drift silently)
- No staleness baseline (doc-check can't detect when they go stale)
- Precedent that undermines the quality pipeline

∀ coverage gap (new subsystem lacks an architecture doc):
- ✅ Propose `/overhaul {service_dir}` to generate it
- ✅ Draft goes to `tmp/prompts/{slug}-architecture-draft.md` as input for the overhaul pass
- ❌ Do NOT write directly to `docs/architecture/`

¬exceptions. If `/doc-check` finds staleness in a subsystem doc, note it in the
commit body ("docs/architecture/{file}.md may need updating via /overhaul") but
do NOT edit the file.

## Appendices — Write Authority

**Invariant**: ∀ files in `docs/architecture/appendices/`: targeted `StrReplace` corrections permitted during `/doc-check`

Appendices are cross-cutting reference docs with no single `/overhaul` target
(configuration, tools, libraries, event system). They are maintained by factual
corrections when `/doc-check` detects staleness — same scope as the former
exception clause, but confined to this directory.

- ✅ Targeted `StrReplace` to fix stale paths, renamed signals, removed config keys
- ❌ Large rewrites or new sections — propose to the user first

## Design Docs — Write Authority

**Invariant**: ∀ files in `docs/architecture/design/`: ¬agent writes unless user-directed

Historical design documents and proposals. Not actively maintained. The agent
must not edit these unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Canonical Reference

`docs/architecture/` is the single source of AI-readable architecture documentation.
It is indexed into RAG and consumed by consultation models.

### Subsystem docs (`docs/architecture/*.md`)

| File | Covers | Overhaul target |
|---|---|---|
| `overview.md` | System-level: services, roles, request flow | — (system-level) |
| `stargate.md` | Stargate internals: proxy, routing, lifecycle | `services/universal-stargate/` |
| `gateway.md` | Gateway: workers, model management, inference | `services/_universal-llm-gateway/` |
| `federation.md` | Federation: roles, routing, telemetry, config | `systems/federation/` |
| `routing.md` | Routing + capacity: feasibility, admission, sticky | `systems/routing/` + `systems/proxy/` |
| `pipeline-system.md` | Pipelines: DAG, handlers, registry, events | `systems/pipeline/` |
| `handlers.md` | Doc-generate pipeline handlers | `pipelines/doc_generate/handlers/` |

